      "problem": "Find the points of intersection of the parabola ${y}^{2}=-8(x-16)$ with the $y$-axis.",
      "worked_solution": "When the parabola intersects the $y$-axis, we must have $x=0.$ So, we set $x=0$ and solve the resulting equation for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =-8(0-16) \\\\ {y}^{2} & =128 \\\\ y & =\\pm \\sqrt{128} \\\\ y & =\\pm 8\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parabola intersects the $y$-axis at $(0,8\\sqrt{2})$ and $(0,-8\\sqrt{2}).$",
